==English==

===Etymology===
{{etyl|enm}} ''hemlok, hemeluc'', from {{etyl|ang}} ''hymlīc(e)'' 'hemlock, bryony, convulvus', literally 'hops-like', from {{term|hymele|lang=ang}} 'hop-vine', from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{recons|humalaz|lang=gem-pro}}, {{recons|humalōn|lang=gem-pro}} (cf. {{etyl|non|-}} {{term|humall|lang=non}}, {{etyl|gml|-}} {{term|homele|lang=gml}}), from Sarmato-Scythian *''haumala'' (compare [[Ossetian]] ''xumællæg'' 'hops'), diminutive of *''hauma'' 'ephedra; juice' (compare {{etyl|ae|-}} ''haoma'', [[Baluchi]] ''hum'', {{etyl|fa|-}} {{term|hōm}}), from {{etyl|iir-pro|en}} {{recons|sauma|lang=iir-pro}} (compare [[Sanskrit]] ''soma''), from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{recons|seue-|lang=ine-pro}} 'to suck; juice'. More at [[suck]].

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun}}

# Any of several [[poisonous]] [[umbellifer]]ous [[plant]]s, of the genera {{taxlink|Conium|genus}} ({{taxlink|Conium maculatum|species}} and {{taxlink|Conium chaerophylloides|species}}) and {{taxlink|Cicuta|genus}}
# The [[poison]] obtained from these plants.
# Any of several [[coniferous]] [[tree]]s, of the genus ''[[Tsuga]]'', that grow in [[North America]]; the [[wood]] of such trees.

